\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Main result: Pairwise vs.\ Likert ATE vs.\ Binarized Likert across 9 judge$\times $benchmark conditions. Continuous Likert ATE is non-significant in all 9 cells. Binarized Likert is non-significant in all 9 cells (2 approach $p{<}0.10$: GPT-4o$\times $AlpacaEval $p{=}0.108$; Gemini$\times $LLMBar $p{=}0.098$). Pairwise comparison detects significance in 2 cells and a trend in 1.}}{5}{table.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:main_sensitivity}{{3}{5}{Main result: Pairwise vs.\ Likert ATE vs.\ Binarized Likert across 9 judge$\times $benchmark conditions. Continuous Likert ATE is non-significant in all 9 cells. Binarized Likert is non-significant in all 9 cells (2 approach $p{<}0.10$: GPT-4o$\times $AlpacaEval $p{=}0.108$; Gemini$\times $LLMBar $p{=}0.098$). Pairwise comparison detects significance in 2 cells and a trend in 1}{table.3}{}}
